[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2510575678","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99378#issuecomment-2510575678","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99378","id":2510575678,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VpFg-","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-02T04:51:48Z","updated_at":"2024-12-02T04:51:48Z","body":"> In both scenarios, you have to keep in mind that the adaptive icon is only used for api 26 and above; for apis lower than 26 (our min is 21), the apk uses the png mipmap resources and with your proposed fix, the manifest declaration will no longer match those png resources.\r\n\r\nSorry I don't understand it, isn't our current implementation similar. I will admit I haven't tested with api 26 and older devices but I don't anticipate any issues. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/c8aca3568ff9d40940fc0da8d99913dbb38328bc/platform/android/java/app/AndroidManifest.xml#L21\r\n\r\n> For the gradle build, you'll need to update icon.xml to add / remove the monochrome tag based on whether the user specified a monochrome icon or not.\r\n\r\nThis approach aligns with what I was previously doing before resorting to directly modifying the file in the Manifest. I’ll switch to using this method instead.\r\n\r\n> If a monochrome icon is specified, then themed_icon.xml data should be retrieved from the apk, and used to overwrite icon.xml data similarly to how we overwrite the png resource data in\r\n\r\nThis is a great idea, I can just overwrite it :D. I will update the PR to use this method.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2510575678/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2510583154","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99378#issuecomment-2510583154","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99378","id":2510583154,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VpHVy","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-02T04:59:43Z","updated_at":"2024-12-02T04:59:43Z","body":"> > In both scenarios, you have to keep in mind that the adaptive icon is only used for api 26 and above; for apis lower than 26 (our min is 21), the apk uses the png mipmap resources and with your proposed fix, the manifest declaration will no longer match those png resources.\r\n> \r\n> Sorry I don't understand it, isn't our current implementation similar. I will admit I haven't tested with api 26 and older devices but I don't anticipate any issues.\r\n> \r\nIn this version of the PR, the presence of a monochrome icon changes the `android:icon` declaration in both the gradle & legacy builds to `android:icon=\"@mipmap/themed_icon\"`.\r\nThe issue with that is that `@mipmap/themed_icon` does not match any of the `png` resources in the `mipmap` folders, and so on devices running api less than 26, the icon resource will not be resolvable.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2510583154/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2510589148","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99378#issuecomment-2510589148","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99378","id":2510589148,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VpIzc","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-02T05:05:35Z","updated_at":"2024-12-02T05:05:35Z","body":"> > > In both scenarios, you have to keep in mind that the adaptive icon is only used for api 26 and above; for apis lower than 26 (our min is 21), the apk uses the png mipmap resources and with your proposed fix, the manifest declaration will no longer match those png resources.\r\n> > \r\n> > \r\n> > Sorry I don't understand it, isn't our current implementation similar. I will admit I haven't tested with api 26 and older devices but I don't anticipate any issues.\r\n> \r\n> In this version of the PR, the presence of a monochrome icon changes the `android:icon` declaration in both the gradle & legacy builds to `android:icon=\"@mipmap/themed_icon\"`. The issue with that is that `@mipmap/themed_icon` does not match any of the `png` resources in the `mipmap` folders, and so on devices running api less than 26, the icon resource will not be resolvable.\r\n\r\nNow I understand, it would be an issue if a user enables monochrome and then uses the app on an older device and due to absence of icon App will falback to default Android icon. Thanks for clarifying!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2510589148/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized